From 92eae558e1bb8219b223cca996278a2315baf0d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brunduk <nikolai.viktorovich@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 18:45:50 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] d/wmr: extend the left-hand reflection to the accelerometer
 (coherent frame for fusion)

T207 reconciliation: the two hands' factory Rt mountings differ by ~178.6deg about Y
(all matrices proper -- no recoverable factory reflection), and the numerically
derived left-to-right correction is exactly diag(1,-1,1) on BOTH post-calibration
sensor vectors. 0062 negated only the gyro, feeding m_imu_3dof inconsistent
conventions: the gravity correction (accel-driven) fought the corrected gyro --
the wearer's 'still wrong' with the gyro-only fix. Same gate, both sensors.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/xrt/drivers/wmr/wmr_controller_hp.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/xrt/drivers/wmr/wmr_controller_hp.c b/src/xrt/drivers/wmr/wmr_controller_hp.c
index 3f95c3b46..6982acc23 100644
--- a/src/xrt/drivers/wmr/wmr_controller_hp.c
+++ b/src/xrt/drivers/wmr/wmr_controller_hp.c
@@ -405,6 +405,17 @@ wmr_controller_hp_packet_parse(struct wmr_controller_hp *ctrl, const unsigned ch
 	if (wcb->base.device_type == XRT_DEVICE_TYPE_LEFT_HAND_CONTROLLER &&
 	    debug_get_bool_option_wmr_controller_left_yaw_gyro_invert()) {
 		last_input->imu.gyro.y = -last_input->imu.gyro.y;
+		// The accel MUST get the same reflection (2026-08-17, T207 reconciliation
+		// analysis): the factory Rt matrices of the two hands differ by ~178.6 deg
+		// about Y (computed from the 0063 determinant log; all matrices proper, so
+		// no factory reflection exists to recover), and the numerically-derived
+		// left-to-right correction is exactly diag(1,-1,1) applied to BOTH
+		// post-calibration sensor vectors. Negating only the gyro fed m_imu_3dof
+		// two INCONSISTENT conventions -- the gravity correction (driven by this
+		// accel) then fights the corrected gyro, which is what the wearer felt as
+		// still-wrong with the gyro-only fix active. Same gate, both sensors,
+		// coherent frame.
+		last_input->imu.acc.y = -last_input->imu.acc.y;
 	}
 
 	uint32_t prev_ticks = last_input->imu.timestamp_ticks & UINT32_C(0xFFFFFFFF);
